    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4160893": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Trainer. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Assistant Athletic Trainer. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $49,743 Degree Required: Bachelor's degree in a related field from a regionally accredited college or university Required Qualifications: Current NATA BOC Certification Current Adult CPR, AED, and First Aid certification Eligible for AT licensure in the State of Idaho Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Proficient in modalities, taping, bracing, and wound care. Communication skills with co-workers, student athletes, coaches, and other healthcare providers. Manual therapy experience and proficiency. First responder capabilities. Proficient in rehabilitation progressions. Ability to teach student AT's as a preceptor. Experience in collegiate athletics. Responsibilities: Specific responsibilities include but are not limited to: Supervise practice and game preparation, competition coverage, design and implement rehabilitation programs, ensuring that all activities are conducted appropriately. Document injuries and rehabilitation for use in preparing and presenting reports and in evaluating recovery of injured athletes. Follow protocols to ensure prompt and appropriate responses when injuries occur. Provide teaching and direction to undergraduate and graduate athletic training students. Prepare reports and serve as a liaison for injured athletes with the team physician and other healthcare providers. Assist in the day-to-day operation of the athletic training room. Monitor the use of equipment and facilities to ensure their proper use and athlete compliance with stated rules. Order or report needed repairs as needed and appropriate to ensure the training facility is fully operational and available for use. Complete training to become a P-card manager. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Perform other duties as assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents, or your application may not be considered for review: Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled; however, applications received on or before August 14, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4153235": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Facilities Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director for Facilities Operations. Lewis-Clark State College. Assistant Director for Facilities Operations At Lewis-Clark State College in Lewiston, ID, you'll have the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on a vibrant campus that combines the close-knit feel of a small college with the quality and opportunities of a larger institution. We're seeking a full-time Assistant Director for Facilities Operations to provide leadership for facility operations, maintenance programs, and campus improvement projects. If you're passionate about leading people, improving facilities, and seeing the results of your work throughout the campus community, you'll find a rewarding career here. You'll earn $75,000-$80,000 per year and enjoy an exceptional benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision insurance for employees and dependents, PTO, a 401(k) with company match, sick leave, 11 paid holidays, 8 weeks of paid parental leave, life and disability insurance, HSA/FSA options, Employee Assistance Program, relocation assistance, a free onsite fitness facility, and remarkable tuition benefits for employees and their families. There's a lot to love about this opportunity, so let's dive in. WHAT YOUR DAYS WILL LOOK LIKE Working Monday through Friday from 7:00 AM-4:00 PM, you'll occasionally assist with emergency situations that require evening or weekend support. In this Assistant Director of Facilities Operations position, you will supervise maintenance, custodial, and grounds personnel while coordinating facility repairs, construction projects, contractor activities, and campus improvement efforts. You will manage projects from planning and initiation through completion, including defining project scope, developing schedules and budgets, coordinating resources, tracking progress, and ensuring projects are completed on time and within established requirements. You will manage work orders, help procure materials, establish preventative maintenance programs, support capital projects, ensure compliance with building and accessibility requirements, and collaborate with campus stakeholders to keep operations running smoothly. Your leadership will help create a campus environment that attracts and retains students while supporting faculty and staff. WHY WE STAND OUT For more than a century, LC State has helped students achieve their goals through accessible, high-quality education and a campus culture centered on connection and support. Known for combining academic achievement with hands-on learning experiences, LC State creates an environment where employees are valued, and collaboration thrives. Working here means being part of a dedicated team that plays an important role in supporting student success and strengthening the campus community. For those looking to build a meaningful career with an institution that emphasizes service, growth, and a strong sense of belonging, LC State is a great place to grow professionally. WHO WILL THRIVE HERE? To be considered for this Assistant Director for Facilities Operations role, you'll need: Bachelor's degree in a related field 2+ years of supervisory and leadership experience 2+ years of project management experience Knowledge of building maintenance and operations Knowledge of building codes and regulations Knowledge of EPA and OSHA safety standards Valid driver's license Preferred experience includes skilled trades, construction scheduling, maintenance planning, procurement, employee training, and interpreting construction plans. READY TO APPLY? Please submit the following materials to be considered for review: Cover letter/letter of interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three (3) professional references Unofficial transcripts (official transcripts required upon hire) Open until filled: The posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a criminal background check. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4166908": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for two Assistant Professor positions - one 9-month position and one 11-month position. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $63,000 - $66,000 for the 9-month position; $77,000 - $80,667 for the 11-month position Degree Required: Master's degree in Nursing from a regionally accredited college or university Required Qualifications: Active, unencumbered ID RN license or eligible to attain. Must have current healthcare provider CPR certification and be able to meet health and immunization requirements. Current clinical nursing experience in areas such as population/community health, nursing leadership, and healthcare policy. Detail-oriented, resourceful, excellent interpersonal oral and written communication skills, and able to work autonomously within a collaborative and dynamic faculty group. Ability to use computers, Microsoft Office applications, Canvas Learning Management System, TEAMS, and other instructional technologies. Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate from a regionally accredited college or university. Experience teaching in an undergraduate or graduate nursing program. Experience with curriculum development. Demonstrated ability to advise and mentor students. Experience with online and/ or distance instruction of nursing courses. Responsibilities: These 9-month or 11-month, full-time, tenure-track faculty members will be responsible for teaching face-to-face didactic and clinical nursing courses as assigned for pre-licensure BSN students, for teaching online coursework for RN-BSN students, and/or for teaching online courses for the nursing graduate program. These teaching assignments are a 9-month contract or an 11-month contract with pay and benefits over 12 months. The successful candidate will participate in curriculum design, implementation, evaluation, and revision and will provide support to enrolled program and pre-program students. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, scholarship/professional development, and service activities. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled; however, applications received on or before September 1, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/3694097": {
      "title": "Assistant Teacher",
      "description": "Assistant Teacher. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for an Assistant Teacher. Assistant Teachers are hired on an as-needed basis. This is an open pool posting. Submission of an application does not guarantee employment. Applications are reviewed as needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted if an opportunity becomes available. Hourly Rate: $10.00 - $12.00 based on education Required Qualifications: At least one (1) year of childcare experience 3-6 college credits in early childhood, education, psychology, social work, and/or nursing or a Child Development Associate Responsibilities: The Assistant Teacher is responsible for helping teachers organize and lead the daily activities of infants, toddlers, and pre-kindergarten children, including helping with toileting or diaper changing, cleaning up after children, providing emotional support, and supervising and engaging with children. Application Procedure: Please upload the following documents Cover Letter Resume Name and contact information for 3 professional references This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4230311": {
      "title": "Budget Analyst",
      "description": "Budget Analyst - Lewiston, ID - Lewis-Clark State College Jobs Home Jobs Login Back to all jobs Budget Analyst 01-Oct-2026 to Until Filled (MST) Career & Technical Education 50,000-55,000 per year Salary Full Time Robust benefits package including medical, vision, and dental insurance for employees and dependents; Generous tuition discount which includes $5 per credit for employees and spouses, as well as 50 percent off of tuition for dependent children up to age 26; Sick and Vacation accrual program; 11 paid holidays; 8 weeks paid parental leave; A generously matched retirement; A free onsite fitness facility with a strong wellness program that allows LC State employees to live healthy, balanced lives; and more. Email Me Similar Jobs Email Me This Job LC State invites applications for the position of Budget Analyst. (This position is not remote and is located in Lewiston, Idaho.) Salary and rank are based on experience and qualifications: $50,000 - $55,000. Degree Required: Bachelor's degree in accounting, bookkeeping, or a related field from a regionally accredited college or university. Required Qualifications: Experience in finance and/or budgeting. Excellent ability to organize, plan, and manage complex projects along with a proven ability to work independently and under pressure. Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Power BI). Involvement in an environment that requires maintaining confidentiality of information. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from a regionally accredited college or university in accounting, finance, or equivalent. Experience in an institution of higher education. Working knowledge of Ellucian Colleague Finance module. Experience analyzing information, identifying problems, defining alternatives, and developing recommendations for management/administrators. Responsibilities: Establish the processes for development of the CTE budget and assure those processes are carried out in a timely manner. Perform scenario planning with respect to CTE budget and related funds, including multi-year forecasts and trend analyses. Assist in preparation of tentative, interim, and final budget submissions for the State within established guidelines; review expenditures for programs to ensure proper budget compliance, with specialization in CTE (Funds 12 & 14). Responsibility for general accounting and related business processes of the Career and Technical Education division, including budget to actual analysis, account reconciliation review and journal entry preparation. Assist in the formulation and review of internal controls, policy guidelines, and internal forms. Monitor and prepare all CTE grant invoices, statements and deposits. Ensure that the College complies with state and federal policies and regulations. Communicate clearly and concisely, both orally and in writing. Support campus-wide fiscal operations through the Budget Office. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with those contacted in the course of work, including regular reporting to the CTE Dean and the Office of the Provost. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled; however, applications received on or before October 30, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer. Apply now How would you like to verify your identity? Continue with phone Verify