r Job to What I Do Now Progress to a Higher Job in the Same Field Jump to a New Field of Work You must select a seeking status answer. Job type Job type Full Time Part Time From Home You must select a job type answer. Next powered by Refer.io Refer.io Resources LCSC Website Job Opportunities Share This Job Hiring Software Maintained by isolved Talent Acquisition - © 2026 Refresh Search the FAQ here Go Common Job Questions"
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4223846": {
      "title": "Compliance Officer",
      "description": "Compliance Officer. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Compliance Officer. Salary and rank are based on experience and qualifications: $85,000 - $89,000 Degree Required: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited college or university Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited higher education institution. Demonstrated ability to organize, plan, and manage complex logistics independently and under pressure, while applying sound discretionary decision-making. Strong analytical, writing, and editing skills, with experience evaluating information, identifying problems and alternatives, developing recommendations, and preparing complex documents and official correspondence for diverse audiences. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and the ability to learn and effectively use enterprise, risk management, insurance, and other administrative software systems. Good knowledge of property, casualty, or workers' compensation insurance contracts and related insurance industry procedures; insurance terminology. Experience in interpreting and explaining provisions of insurance policies including coverages, limits, exclusions, and appropriateness of coverage for desired result. Experience in identifying and resolving insurance problems for commercial insurers; explaining technical insurance-related information in common terms; reviewing and interpreting insurance documents; calculating insurance premiums using mathematical analysis and survey techniques. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from a regionally accredited higher education institution. Direct experience working with state or governmental risk management programs, insurance policies, or compliance frameworks. Professional experience in higher education, government, or similarly complex organizational environments. Knowledge of records management and retention practices, including compliance with state or federal regulations. Familiarity with risk management software platforms or insurance tracking tools. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion. Responsibilities: Manage the risk management program for the institution and work collaboratively with the Department of Administration's Risk Management Program to help reduce exposure and control the cost of loss. Serve as the primary institutional liaison for liability insurance, overseeing claims management, certificates of insurance, policy implementation, and renewals to ensure adequate and continuous coverage. Manage and update all institutional insurance policies, including large property, leased and owned vehicles, small property insurance, vehicles, and other policies, utilizing state software systems to maintain accurate records. Coordinate any insurance-related site visits. Develop, implement, and maintain liability waivers for high-risk events and activities, ensuring compliance with institutional and state guidelines. Maintain comprehensive documentation of all risk management activities. Establish and maintain procedures for reporting injuries, property damage, theft, and accidents. This includes working with key campus constituencies to standardize internal and external communication to parties involved with the aforementioned incidents. Administers budgets for Risk Management. Support institutional compliance efforts by assisting with compliance-related activities and coordinating with campus departments, the Chief Compliance Officer, and the Compliance Committee as appropriate, potentially including research and report generation related to compliance issues. Assist in the preparation of state-required compliance reports, internal audit responses, and internal conflict-of-interest responses. Ensure that all Risk Management websites and related webpages are accurate and up to date. Researches and interprets applicable laws, policies, and other regulatory requirements into guidance that informs institutional decision-making to minimize and respond to risk. Provides guidance on risk-related events as they occur, including those that activate the emergency operations structure, which may occur after normal business hours. Supports risk-related tabletop exercises and employee training. Other duties as assigned. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled. The posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/3703931": {
      "title": "Custodian - Day Shift",
      "description": "Custodian - Day Shift. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Custodian. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $15.00 per hour (Hours are 7:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.; Monday - Friday) Required Qualifications: Willingness to: perform duties associated with commercial cleaning, including operating industrial-type cleaning equipment such as high-speed buffers and vacuum cleaners; cleaning restrooms, bath facilities, locker rooms, and similar facilities; moving heavy items such as tables, chairs, and bleachers; and repairing the equipment and related devices. Preferred Qualifications: Experience cleaning in a commercial, educational, or industrial setting. Experience in operating custodial maintenance equipment. Associate's Degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Responsibilities: Cleaning/maintenance: Typical duties: performs heavy-duty cleaning in hospital setting, locker rooms, classrooms, dormitories, and lavatories; cleans, sanitizes, and polishes bath, lavatory, shower, and sink fixtures; dusts, washes, sponge mops; sanitizes, and shampoos furniture, woodwork, walls, windows, and glass items; cleans shades and covers on light fixtures; replaces light bulbs; removes waste and debris from areas; selects products and compounds for cleaning jobs; measures and mixes compounds, disinfectants, and sanitizing agents and applies according to procedures or manufacturers' specifications; orders supplies for custodial closets and stocks with paper products, cleaning compounds and similar items; sweeps, strips, seals, and finishes wood, linoleum, and other floors; washes windows in multi-story buildings; removes and prepares draperies for cleaning; removes adhesives, tiles, and carpet; refinishes floors and prepares them for re-carpeting or special flooring; instructs temporary help. Equipment operation/security: Typical duties: operates heavy-duty scrubbing, buffing, shampooing, vacuuming, and wet/dry pickup equipment; performs preventive maintenance on cleaning equipment; finishes floors using sanders, strippers, and final finishers; uses snow blowers, hysters, airlift platforms, dollies, and carts; replaces belts, brushes, and bearings in power equipment; ensures that floor and building area is secure; verifies doors are locked and lights and appliances are off; reports fire hazards and other emergencies. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
