    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4180947": {
      "title": "Events &amp; Conferences Coordinator",
      "description": "Events &amp; Conferences Coordinator. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Events & Conferences Coordinator. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $50,000 - $55,000 Degree Required: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited college or university Required Qualifications: Two (2) years of experience in event services, conference management, hospitality, marketing, higher education administration, or a related field; Demonstrated experience managing multiple projects and priorities in a fast-paced environment; Experience supervising or leading staff or teams; Experience managing budgets, contracts, and financial transactions; Proficiency with Microsoft Office and business software systems; Hold a valid driver's license Ability to lift up to 50 pounds Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree from a regionally accredited college or university in Higher Education Administration, Business, Communications, Hospitality Management, or a related field; Five (5) years' experience working in higher education event services, conference management, or hospitality operations; Knowledge of facility scheduling systems, CRM platforms, and event management technology; Experience developing marketing strategies and promotional campaigns; Experience supervising staff and implementing operational policies and procedures; Strong understanding of marketing and event/program promotion; and Knowledge of risk management and event compliance practices. Responsibilities: The Events & Conferences Coordinator oversees the operations, facilities, and services of LC State's Events & Conferences program, including the Williams Conference Center (WCC). This position manages event scheduling and facility reservations through 25Live, supervises the event set-up crew, coordinates maintenance and repairs, and ensures a high-quality experience for both internal and external clients. The position also oversees budgets, financial reporting, billing and collections, facility-use processes, compliance requirements, and the annual review of reservable campus spaces and associated fees. The Coordinator will develop and implement business and marketing strategies to expand outside use of LC State facilities and promote Events & Conferences services to campus and community partners through in-person outreach, promotional materials, social media, and conferences. The position provides leadership, mentoring, and coaching to staff; identifies opportunities to improve processes, efficiencies, and policies; and makes recommendations for facility upgrades and modifications. Evening and weekend work, as well as occasional in- and out-of-state travel, may be required. Additional responsibilities include supporting student recruitment and retention initiatives and performing other duties as assigned. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled. The posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/3762681": {
      "title": "Instructor of Diesel Technology",
      "description": "Instructor of Diesel Technology. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Instructor of Diesel Technology (non-tenure track). Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $62,000 Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in related field from an accredited college/university plus three years of current experience in a related field; or Associate degree in a related field from an accredited college/university with five years of current field experience in a related field, or Eight years of current experience in a related field Experience in electrical, powertrains, and hydraulics as it relates to the diesel repair industry. Experience with repair software used in the diesel industry. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in marketing, advertising, and/or recruiting. Experience instructing adult learners and demonstrate multiple methods of assessing student knowledge and skill to teach and advise students in the Diesel Technology program. Experience managing budgets, designing instructional activities, supervising, creating fruitful partnerships, and/or recruiting and retaining students. Preference will be given to applicants with a Class A CDL. Responsibilities: Instructs and supervises students in the Diesel Technology program. Develop, plan, implement, and revise programs and courses, curriculum, and lesson plans. Evaluates student progress in attaining goals and objectives. Maintain lab/shop equipment and program/personal certification requirements; attend faculty and educational meetings. Assist in recruitment, retention, and job placement efforts as well as ensuring safety and security for the program. Work with the program's advisory committee, industry representatives, and employers to facilitate job and internship opportunities. Operate and maintain program budget, contribute to college-wide goals and activities by serving on committees and other institutional activities. Applicants are required to complete CTE teacher training courses for Idaho Teaching Certification. Applicants must be willing to consider non-traditional teaching styles and times, such as online, hybrid, and evening or weekend classes, to expand cohort options. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
