    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/3939053": {
      "title": "Landscape Technician",
      "description": "Landscape Technician. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Landscape Technician (2 openings). Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $16.83 - $18.26 per hour Required Qualifications: At least six months or one season performing related work (Home yard work is not qualifying experience unless it is for a very large and detailed landscape/grounds) Grounds equipment operation, maintenance, and repair. Strong communication skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently, coordinate and facilitate solutions, and analyze and resolve landscape issues. A valid driver's license is required. Preferred Qualifications: Associate's degree Knowledge of plants and soil types. Horticulture and professional landscaping practices. Knowledge of spraying of pesticides and herbicides. Basic pruning & irrigation knowledge. Responsibilities: General grounds maintenance. Grounds equipment operation, maintenance, and repair. Operate equipment: snow blowers, lawn mowers, string trimmers, edgers, leaf blowers, forklifts, aerial lifts, tractors, dollies, carts, hand tools, and other mechanized equipment. Set up bleachers, portable stages and flooring, and tables and chairs for special events. Respond to emerging conditions on campus, assist with leaf and snow removal, and flood water cleanup. Assist other Physical Plant crews as needed. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4224894": {
      "title": "Program Assistant for Student Work Programs",
      "description": "Program Assistant for Student Work Programs. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Program Assistant for Student Work Programs. Salary and rank are based on experience and qualifications: $49,754 - $53,000 Degree Required: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Required Qualifications: Experience with career development, career education, or staff supervision Experience working with databases. Excellent organization, time management, analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master's preferred from a regionally accredited college/university. Work experience in higher education. Experience using situational awareness to provide excellent and adaptable customer service in a variety of situations. Flexibility to work in an open office environment and actively collaborate with other staff members. Responsibilities: Managing the Work Scholar program, Managing the Federal, State, and JOB Work-Study programs, Developing and presenting training materials for aid-based student work programs, Working with internal and external employer partners and supervisors to support student workers, Assisting students and families with general guidance on financial aid and scholarship processes, including completing the FAFSA, scholarship, and other financial forms or documents, Making presentations about financial aid, scholarships, and aid-based work programs to prospective students, current students, and high school counselors, Creating or enhancing correspondence to students. Collaborating on marketing materials that promote the services in Student Financial Services Partnering with other office staff on projects and assignments, Serving on campus committees as needed, and Other duties as assigned. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled; however, applications received on or before October 16, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/3761547": {
      "title": "Program Director of Respiratory Therapy",
      "description": "Program Director of Respiratory Therapy. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Program Director of Respiratory Therapy. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $75,000 - $80,000 Degree Required: Bachelor's degree awarded by an academic institution that is accredited by a regional or national accrediting agency recognized by the U.S. Department of Education (USDE). Required Qualifications: Active, valid, Registered Respiratory Therapy (RRT) credential and current state license Minimum of four (4) years' experience as a Registered Respiratory Therapist with at least two (2) years in clinical respiratory care Minimum of two (2) years' experience teaching either as an appointed faculty member in a CoARC-accredited respiratory care program or as a clinical instructor/preceptor for students of such programs Complete the CoARC Key Personnel Training Program or ability to complete Ability to manage supply inventory Utilize Microsoft Office programs such as Word, Excel, and Access database The successful candidate will be detail-oriented, resourceful, and able to work autonomously within a collaborative and dynamic faculty group Idaho State CTE teaching certification or ability to obtain within 3 years Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from a nationally accredited institution Experience with curriculum development Experience with program accreditation Experience teaching in a clinical lab setting Experience recruiting, advising, and mentoring students Demonstrated ability to collaborate and develop strong internal and external partnerships Demonstrated ability to provide direction and oversight to staff/students/student workers Responsibilities: The Program Director for the Respiratory Therapy program is a 12-month full-time non-tenure track professional staff member who will manage all aspects of the Respiratory Therapy program. The Program Director must provide effective leadership for the program, including, but not limited to, responsibility for communication, ongoing program planning and assessment, and fiscal management. The Program Director's administrative responsibilities include: fiscal planning; program planning and development; ongoing review and analysis of all program activities; ensuring that, in all aspects, the program meets the requirements of the accreditation Standards. Educational responsibilities include continuous curriculum development and review as well as teaching. The Program Director must work with the Director of Clinical Education to ensure that clinical education for program students is coordinated with didactic and laboratory activities and is sufficient to meet program outcomes required by the Standards. The Program Director manages all clinical lab functions, including inventory management (monitoring and ordering of all student supplies), set-up for all lab sessions, and is an instructor for the didactic and lab courses needed for the Respiratory Therapy program completion. This position sets up, maintains, and monitors all equipment and testing activities. This position will plan, evaluate, budget, and assist in the selection of adjunct faculty and staff for the Respiratory Therapy program. Maintain CoARC Respiratory Therapy accreditation. Maintain professional development requirements. Coordinate the schedule of the Respiratory Therapy program offerings. Participate on the Respiratory Therapy Advisory Committee, attend meetings, and prepare and submit appropriate CTE reports. Maintain CTE instructor certification requirements. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/3761521": {
      "title": "Program Director of Surgical Technology",
      "description": "Program Director of Surgical Technology. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Program Director of Surgical Technology. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $75,000 - $80,000 Degree Required: Associate degree awarded and concentrated in surgical technology by an institution that is accredited by a nationally recognized programmatic accreditation agency. Required Qualifications: Possess a credential in the field of surgical technology through a national certification program that is accredited by the National Commission on Certifying Agencies (NCCA) Have a minimum total of five (5) years of experience, either in the operating room scrub role or as an instructor in surgical technology, or a combination of both, within the past ten (10) years Have documented education or experience in instructional methodology, curriculum design/development, and program planning Possess experience/training as an educator Utilize Microsoft Office programs such as Word, Excel, and Access database The successful candidate will be detail-oriented, resourceful, and able to work autonomously within a collaborative and dynamic faculty group Idaho State CTE teaching certification or ability to obtain within 3 years. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's or Master's degree from a nationally accredited institution Experience with program accreditation Experience teaching in a clinical lab setting Experience recruiting, advising, and mentoring students Demonstrated ability to collaborate and develop strong internal and external partnerships Demonstrated ability to provide direction and oversight to staff/students/student workers Responsibilities: The Program Director for the Surgical Technology program is a 12-month full-time non-tenure track professional staff member who will manage all aspects of the Surgical Technology program. The Program Director must be responsible for all aspects of the program, including but not limited to: 1) Administration, organization, supervision of the program; and 2) Continuous quality review and improvement of the program; and 3) Academic oversight, including curriculum planning and development The Program Director should pursue ongoing formal training designed to maintain and upgrade his/her professional, instructional, and administrative capabilities. The Program Director should participate in and ARC/STSA sponsored accreditation workshop at least once every five years. The Program Director manages all clinical lab functions, including inventory management (monitoring and ordering of all student supplies), set-up for all lab sessions, and is an instructor for the didactic and lab courses needed for Surgical Technology program completion. This position sets up, maintains, and monitors all equipment and testing activities. This person will oversee and coordinate schedules with a clinical coordinator, possible adjunct instructors, and student lab workers. This position will plan, evaluate, budget, and assist in the selection of adjunct faculty and staff for the Surgical Technology program. Maintain CAAHEP Surgical Technology accreditation. Maintain professional development requirements. Coordinate the schedule of Surgical Technology program offerings. Participate in the Surgical Technology Technical Advisory Committee, attend meetings, and prepare and submit appropriate CTE reports. Maintain CTE instructor certification requirements. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4153164": {
      "title": "Scheduling &amp; Systems Specialist",
      "description": "Scheduling &amp; Systems Specialist. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Scheduling & Systems Specialist. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $49,743 Degree Required: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited college or university Required Qualifications: Ability to troubleshoot technology issues and comfortable working with databases Experience working in an office, excellent communication and customer service skills Ability to organize resources, establish priorities, and meet deadlines Ability to work independently and cooperatively on multiple projects with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail Proficient in Microsoft Office programs, specifically Excel, strong computer skills, and ability to navigate various databases Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree from a regionally accredited college or university Experience working in a higher education institution Experience with Student Information System Experience with CourseLeaf CLSS/CAT/CIM Experience with Series 25Live software Responsibilities: Assist faculty/staff/students in a broad range of services in the Warrior OneStop Co-coordinate registration, scheduling, programs, and courses Manage CourseLeaf CLSS, 25Live, Perceptive Content, Dual Enroll course uploads, and Student Planning systems Assist the Associate Director of Admissions/Registrar & Records with Colleague rules, cohorts, and functions Produce and edit class and time schedules and scheduling of classes Process dual credit registrations and drops Register Teacher In-Service student applications Process Individualized Study student applications Run reports and provide quality control metrics Coordinate software updates/testing for the office Process a variety of forms received in the office such as add/drop, PIFs, withdraws, name/address change Other duties as assigned Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled; however, applications received on or before August 8, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/1268301": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "Security Officer. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for Security Officer. Security Officers are hired on an as-needed basis. This is an open pool posting. Submission of an application does not guarantee employment. Applications are reviewed as security needs arise, and qualified applicants may be contacted if an opportunity becomes available. Hourly Rate: $15.00 - $16.00 (up to 20 hours per week) Required Qualifications: Valid driver's license with a clean driving record Ability to make quick, sound decisions and apply common sense calmly and professionally in emergencies Able to work in inclement weather, be on your feet for up to eight (8) hours, and lift forty (40) pounds Desired Skills: Dependable, trustworthy Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written Able to follow directions Works well alone or in a team setting Affable, observant, and takes pride in this responsibility to our campus community Application Procedure: Please upload the following documents Cover Letter Resume Name and contact information for 3 professional references This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4037919": {
      "title": "Site Program Administrator - Medical Lab Technology",
      "description": "Site Program Administrator - Medical Lab Technology. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Site Program Administrator - Medical Lab Technology. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $75,000 - $80,000. Degree Required: Bachelor's degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Required Qualifications: ASCP BOC or ASCPi BOC generalist certification as a medical laboratory scientist. At least one year of experience in medical laboratory science education to include knowledge of: education methods, program assessment and administration, and certification/licensure procedures. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with curriculum development Experience with program accreditation Experience teaching in a clinical lab setting Experience recruiting, advising, and mentoring students Demonstrated ability to collaborate and develop strong internal and external partnerships Demonstrated ability to provide direction and oversight to staff/students/student workers Responsibilities: The Site Program Administrator is responsible for: • Coordinating teaching and clinical/applied learning education • Evaluating program effectiveness • Maintaining appropriate communications with the program director • Providing leadership and oversight of the MLT program operations, including program development, curriculum, budgeting, and staff management • Facilitating curriculum development and revision processes in collaboration with the Idaho Consortium for Medical Laboratory Technology Education, and in alignment with industry standards and accreditation requirements • Collaborating with industry partners, healthcare facilities, and employers to ensure programs meet workforce demands • Facilitating campus program approval processes • Coordinating the schedule of MLT program offerings • Managing all clinical lab functions, including inventory management (monitoring and ordering of all student supplies), set-up for all lab sessions, and instructing didactic and lab courses needed for MLT program completion • The setup, maintenance, and monitoring of all equipment and testing activities • Advising NHS - CTE Assistant Chair on issues relative to MLT program • Coordinating with NHS - CTE Assistant Chair to align MLT program operations and facilitate collaboration amongst allied health programs • Assisting in the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of other allied health CTE programs • Teaching in the MLT program • Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4194430": {
      "title": "Small Business Support Specialist I",
      "description": "Small Business Support Specialist I. Lewis-Clark State College. Idaho Small Business Development Center is seeking a Small Business Support Specialist 1. This is a part-time, no benefits position with an hourly rate of $18.00. Degree Requirement: Bachelor's degree in Business (or closely related field) or be actively working toward completing a Business degree (or closely related field) from an accredited institution. Required Qualifications: Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) Perform a variety of office support functions, including but not limited to communicating verbally and in writing, creating reports, and filling out forms. Respond to inquiries and explain program services, policies, and procedures to current and potential clients. Attention to detail. Responsibilities: Provide administrative support for Idaho SBDC staff, including with department travel and department purchasing. Provide customer service to clients, the public, the Idaho SBDC, Lewis-Clark State College, and other organizations. File, scan, make copies, prepare and proof documents and correspondence, pick up and deliver mail to/from Lewis-Clark State College's mailroom. Answer the phone and respond to e-mails, provide information, forward e-mails and calls, send out surveys, leave messages, and assist walk-in clients as needed. When invited, assist Business Consultants with client projects concerning various business topics. Maintain Center IC client database. Input new clients, narratives, trainings, impacts, student projects, and create reports. Check calendars and confirm appointments and workshop attendance. Use Microsoft Office programs, including Outlook, Word, Excel, Publisher, and also Canvas to perform duties. Coordinate work with other staff, interns, and students. Attend and participate in meetings and trainings related to the position. Keep track of hours worked and input on state time card system. When invited, observe and participate with experienced Business Consultant(s) during appointments with selected clients. Analyze issues, identify opportunities, and help clients regarding business management, marketing, accounting, operations, planning, leadership, regulations, and other business operations. Conduct research and work on projects in order to assist clients, such as helping clients with business plans, marketing plans, cash flow projections, and other business projects. Help center meet Idaho SBDC annual goals including the following: Client Business Starts, Capital Raised, Jobs Created, and Sales Growth. Maintain strict confidentiality of all client information. Application Procedure: Please upload the following documents Cover Letter Resume Three Professional References This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4116089": {
      "title": "Small Business Support Specialist II",
      "description": "Small Business Support Specialist II. Lewis-Clark State College. Idaho Small Business Development Center is seeking a Small Business Support Specialist II. This is a part-time, no benefits position with an hourly rate of $27.00. Degree Requirement: Bachelor's degree in Business (or closely related field) from an accredited institution or equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience required. Required Qualifications: Experience with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) At least three years of small business ownership, management, lending, business consulting, or an equivalent combination of knowledge, skill, and experience. Responsibilities: Provide administrative support for Idaho SBDC staff, including with department travel and department purchasing. Provide customer service to clients, the public, the Idaho SBDC, Lewis-Clark State College, and other organizations. File, scan, make copies, prepare and proof documents and correspondence, pick up and deliver mail to/from Lewis-Clark State College's mailroom. Answer the phone and respond to e-mails, provide information, forward e-mails and calls, send out surveys, leave messages, and assist walk-in clients as needed. When invited, assist Business Consultants with client projects concerning various business topics. Maintain Center IC client database. Input new clients, narratives, trainings, impacts, student projects, and create reports. Check calendars and confirm appointments and workshop attendance. Use Microsoft Office programs, including Outlook, Word, Excel, Publisher, and also Canvas to perform duties. Coordinate work with other staff, interns, and students. Attend and participate in meetings and trainings related to the position. Keep track of hours worked and input on state time card system. When invited, observe and participate with experienced Business Consultant(s) during appointments with selected clients. Analyze issues, identify opportunities, and help clients regarding business management, marketing, accounting, operations, planning, leadership, regulations, and other business operations. Conduct research and work on projects in order to assist clients, such as helping clients with business plans, marketing plans, cash flow projections, and other business projects. Develop, coordinate, and provide business training workshops as needed. Help center meet Idaho SBDC annual goals including the following: Client Business Starts, Capital Raised, Jobs Created, and Sales Growth. Maintain strict confidentiality of all client information. Application Procedure: Please upload the following documents Cover Letter Resume Three Professional References This position is open until filled. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    },
    "https://lcsc.applicantpro.com/jobs/4136037": {
      "title": "Sonography Program Director/Instructor",
      "description": "Sonography Program Director/Instructor. Lewis-Clark State College. LC State invites applications for the position of Sonography Program Director/Instructor. Salary and rank based on experience and qualifications: $75,000 - $80,000. Degree required: Bachelor's degree in the radiologic science field from a regionally accredited college or university. Required Qualifications: Possess a credential in the field of registered sonographer Minimum of two (2) years of experience as a registered sonographer in the sonography field Demonstrated ability to utilize Microsoft Office programs such as Word, Excel, and Access database The successful candidate will be detail-oriented, resourceful, and able to work autonomously within a collaborative and dynamic faculty group Idaho State CTE teaching certification or ability to obtain within 3 years. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from a regionally accredited college or university. Documented education or experience in instructional methodology, curriculum design/development, and program planning Experience with program accreditation Experience teaching in a clinical lab setting Experience recruiting, advising, and mentoring students Demonstrated ability to collaborate and develop strong internal and external partnerships Demonstrated ability to provide direction and oversight to staff/students/student workers Responsibilities: The Program Director for the Sonography program is a 12-month full-time non-tenure-track professional staff member/ Instructor who will manage all aspects of the Sonography program. The Program Director must provide effective leadership for the program including, but not limited to, responsibility for communication, ongoing program planning and assessment, and fiscal management. The Program Director's administrative responsibilities include: fiscal planning; program planning and development; ongoing review and analysis of all program activities; ensuring that, in all aspects, the program meets the requirements of the accreditation Standards. Educational responsibilities include curriculum development and ongoing review in addition to teaching. The Program Director manages all clinical lab functions including inventory management (monitoring and ordering of all student supplies), set-up for all lab sessions, and is an instructor for the didactic and lab courses needed for Sonography program completion. This position sets up, maintains, and monitors all equipment and testing activities. This position will plan, evaluate, budget, and assist in the selection of adjunct faculty and staff for the Sonography program. Maintain professional development requirements. Coordinate the schedule of Sonography program offerings. Collaborate with industry partners, healthcare facilities, and employers to ensure the program meets workforce demands, participating on the Sonography program Technical Advisory Committee. Attend meetings and prepare and submit appropriate CTE reports. Maintain CTE instructor certification requirements. Additional duties include direct and indirect activities to support recruitment and retention of students. Application Procedure: Please upload all of the following documents or your application may not be considered for review. Cover Letter/Letter of Interest Resume/Curriculum Vitae Contact Information or Letters for three (3) Professional References Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts requested upon hire) This position is open until filled; however, applications received on or before July 20, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check and may also be subject to an education verification. LC State is an EEO/VETS employer."
    }
  },
